{"type":"text","timestamp":1787396578071,"sessionID":"ses_fd6df1da6ffed1G2gMnO138EZv","part":{"id":"prt_029235175001vOlitW6xYILAhm","messageID":"msg_029234d96001Oet0aCDjVLsHJa","sessionID":"ses_fd6df1da6ffed1G2gMnO138EZv","type":"text","text":"Good! So the parsing should work. Let me trace through manually what should happen:\n\n- Pattern 1: `(true,  _,     _)` matches all combinations with first=true → (T,T,T), (T,T,F), (T,F,T), (T,F,F)\n- Pattern 2: `(false, true,  _)` matches all combinations with first=false, second=true → (F,T,T), (F,T,F)\n- Pattern 3: `(false, false, false)` matches (F,F,F)\n- Pattern 4: `(false, false, true)` matches (F,F,T)\n\nSo we cover: (T,T,T), (T,T,F), (T,F,T), (T,F,F), (F,T,T), (F,T,F), (F,F,F), (F,F,T) = all 8 combinations. Should be exhaustive!\n\nThe problem might be in how I'm parsing the tuple elements. Let me check the spacing:","time":{"start":1787396575605,"end":1787396578067}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787396581206,"sessionID":"ses_fd6df1da6ffed1G2gMnO138EZv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01BzqAWhS4BfQ5LemtUqzvbh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45 && python3 -c \"\ndef pattern_matches_value(pattern: str, value):\n    if not pattern.startswith('('):\n        return False\n    \n    pattern = pattern[1:-1]  # Remove outer parens\n    pattern_parts = [p.strip() for p in pattern.split(',')]\n    \n    print(f'Pattern {repr(pattern)} -> parts: {pattern_parts}')\n    print(f'Value: {value}, len={len(value)}')\n    print(f'Parts len: {len(pattern_parts)}')\n    \n    if len(pattern_parts) != len(value):\n        return False\n    \n    for p, v in zip(pattern_parts, value):\n        print(f'  Checking {repr(p)} vs {v}')\n        if p == '_':\n            continue\n        elif p == 'true' and v != True:\n            return False\n        elif p == 'false' and v != False:\n            return False\n        else:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n\nresult = pattern_matches_value('(true,  _,     _)', (True, True, True))\nprint(f'Result: {result}')\n\"\n"},"output":"Pattern 'true,  _,     _' -> parts: ['true', '_', '_']\nValue: (True, True, True), len=3\nParts len: 3\n  Checking 'true' vs True\nResult: False\n","metadata":{"output":"Pattern 'true,  _,     _' -> parts: ['true', '_', '_']\nValue: (True, True, True), len=3\nParts len: 3\n  Checking 'true' vs True\nResult: False\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45 && python3 -c \"\ndef pattern_matches_value(pattern: str, value):\n    if not pattern.startswith('('):\n        return False\n    \n    pattern = pattern[1:-1]  # Remove outer parens\n    pattern_parts = [p.strip() for p in pattern.split(',')]\n    \n    print(f'Pattern {repr(pattern)} -> parts: {pattern_parts}')\n    print(f'Value: {value}, len={len(value)}')\n    print(f'Parts len: {len(pattern_parts)}')\n    \n    if len(pattern_parts) != len(value):\n        return False\n    \n    for p, v in zip(pattern_parts, value):\n        print(f'  Checking {repr(p)} vs {v}')\n        if p == '_':\n            continue\n        elif p == 'true' and v != True:\n            return False\n        elif p == 'false' and v != False:\n            return False\n        else:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n\nresult = pattern_matches_value('(true,  _,     _)', (True, True, True))\nprint(f'Result: {result}')\n\"\n","time":{"start":1787396581181,"end":1787396581184}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_029235b16001FeaviYQWyCqpX9","sessionID":"ses_fd6df1da6ffed1G2gMnO138EZv","messageID":"msg_029234d96001Oet0aCDjVLsHJa"}}
