{"type":"text","timestamp":1787396632258,"sessionID":"ses_fd6df1da6ffed1G2gMnO138EZv","part":{"id":"prt_029241ac8001yzvYjSJh7gUWjF","messageID":"msg_029241664001b8Gz2QOofFiAmR","sessionID":"ses_fd6df1da6ffed1G2gMnO138EZv","type":"text","text":"Excellent! Let me create a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented `switchcheck`, a diagnostic checker for the .bs programming language's switch statement validation. The implementation:\n\n**Diagnostics checked:**\n1. **switch_inexhaustive** - Reports when a switch over a closed type doesn't cover all variants (e.g., tuple of bools)\n2. **unreachable_arm** - Reports when a switch arm duplicates an earlier pattern\n3. **rebinding** - Reports when a bare parameter name repeats in a pattern (would rebind the parameter)\n4. **return_not_declared** - Reports when a switch arm returns a value of a different type than declared\n\n**Key features:**\n- Parses .bs file syntax to extract module names, type definitions, and function signatures\n- Handles both single-value switches (on typed values) and tuple switches\n- Exhaustiveness checking for boolean tuples (all 2^n combinations must be covered)\n- Exhaustiveness checking for closed user-defined types (all variants must be matched)\n- Support for open types like `atom` where catch-all `_` is allowed\n- Support for guards in switch arms (`when` conditions)\n- Return type inference from atom literals (`:atom`) and numeric literals (`123`)\n\n**Test results:**\nAll 8 test cases pass correctly:\n- c01: Exhaustive closed type → no output ✓\n- c02: Exhaustive with catch-all over open atom type → no output ✓\n- c03: Inexhaustive (missing variant) → `switch_inexhaustive` ✓\n- c04: Unreachable arm (duplicate pattern) → `unreachable_arm` ✓\n- c05: Exhaustive boolean tuple → no output ✓\n- c06: Inexhaustive boolean tuple → `switch_inexhaustive` ✓\n- c07: Guarded patterns covering all ints → no output ✓\n- c08: Return type mismatch → `return_not_declared` ✓\n\nThe executable `./switchcheck` is ready and passes all test cases.","time":{"start":1787396627145,"end":1787396632235}}}
